<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="section-the-complete-ordered-field" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>
    The Complete Ordered Field
  </title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      In the previous section, we gave an explicit and detailed construction of the real number system <m> \R </m>. In this section, we give an alternative and non-constructive characterization of <m> \R </m> as the unique <term> Dedekind complete </term> <term> ordered field </term>. This will set the stage for abandoning the Dedekind cut perspective in favor of an abstract conception of the properties of the real number system.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="./subsection-the-ordered-field-axioms.ptx"/>

  <xi:include href="./subsection-dedekind-completeness.ptx"/>

  <conclusion>
    <p>
      In the next section, we will construct various extensions of the real number system <m> \R </m>. In particular, we will see the <term> extended real numbers </term>, the <term> complex numbers </term>, and the <term> quaternions </term>.
    </p>
  </conclusion>

  <xi:include href="./exercises-the-complete-ordered-field.ptx"/>

  <xi:include href="./problems-the-complete-ordered-field.ptx"/>
</section>
